        <p class="profile-detail-region">Life · Sub-Saharan Africa</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Nelson Mandela</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1918 CE – 2013 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">18 July 1918, in the village of Mvezo in Umtata, then part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-province">Cape Province</a>; a Xhosa of a cadet branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thembu">Thembu</a> royal family, son of the chief Gadla Henry Mphakanyiswa Mandela and Nosekeni Fanny</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">5 December 2013, aged 95, at his home in Houghton, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannesburg">Johannesburg</a>, after a prolonged respiratory infection; state funeral on 15 December in Qunu</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Who they were</span><span class="info-stat-val">Lawyer; national president of the ANC Youth League (from 1950); co-founder and chairman of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umkhonto-we-sizwe">Umkhonto we Sizwe</a> (1961); President of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-national-congress">African National Congress</a> (1991–1997); President of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> (1994–1999); Secretary-General of the Non-Aligned Movement (1998–1999)</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">leading the struggle against apartheid; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rivonia-trial">Rivonia Trial</a> and the &quot;I Am Prepared to Die&quot; speech; 27 years in prison; negotiating the end of apartheid with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/f-w-de-klerk">F. W. de Klerk</a>; becoming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>'s first black head of state; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/truth-and-reconciliation-commission-south-africa">Truth and Reconciliation Commission</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a></span></div>
